  "body": "## Summary\n\nPart of #35.\n\nThis PR records the S-CORE `eclipse-score/communication` Rust API issue queue (baseline\n`381d43dec900ab6a9076f3f30e7bfbdee019e26e`). It adds one folder per issue under\n`contributions/issues/eclipse-score/communication/`, a shared `rust-api-queue/` folder,\n12 `registry.json` entries and one `contributions/README.md` bullet.\n\nNothing here has been submitted to S-CORE. The folders hold everything needed to open the\nupstream PRs later.\n\n| Issue | Folder content | Upstream readiness |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| #1261 async stream of new services | patch, branch bundle, PR draft, evidence | Linux checks pass; scope and allocation questions for maintainers not yet posted |\n| #250 `FindServiceSpecifier::Any` | patch, bundle, PR draft, evidence | Linux checks pass |\n| #560 subscription state APIs | patch, bundle, PR draft, evidence | Linux checks pass; suggested first upstream PR |\n| #781 `MethodInArgPtr` | draft patch, bundle, evidence | Draft; ABI/ownership unsettled |\n| #490 mock runtime | draft patch, bundle, evidence | Draft; never built successfully |\n| #173, #1264, #1263, #782, #1062 | evidence and assessment | No code change |\n| #794 | evidence | Handled upstream by the maintainer |\n| #741 | evidence | Not implemented |\n\nThe #1265 folder already exists on `main` and is unchanged.\n\n## What reviewers should check\n\n- **Each issue `README.md`:** status, measured results and open items stated accurately,\n  with no acceptance claimed.\n- **`pr-title.txt` / `pr-description.md`** (#1261, #250, #560, #781, #490): ready to paste\n  into an upstream PR.\n- **`registry.json`:** 12 additions only; existing entries and formatting are unchanged.\n- **Size:** about 200 MB. Raw Fabro event streams are stored as `events.jsonl.zst`, with each\n  original SHA-256 recorded in `compressed-evidence.json`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- The new entries pass `scripts/verify_contributions.py`'s checks (3,054 files across 12 folder\n  manifests, patch hashes, upstream snapshots), and the shared folder's 1,311-file manifest\n  verifies.\n- The full verifier still stops at the existing `eclipse-score/inc_diagnostics#16` entry\n  (registry `2026-10-06` vs snapshot `2026-10-04`). That fails on `main` too and is not changed here.\n- Every copied evidence file was re-hashed against its original sealed manifest: 5,707 entries,\n  0 mismatches, with event streams decompressed for the check.\n- Each patch matches its sealed source change (`git patch-id`). Each branch merges into current\n  communication `main` (`e073dede`) without textual conflict; the merged results were not built.\n- A credential-pattern scan of all added files, including decompressed event streams, found nothing.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Code was drafted by agents (DeepSeek V4 Flash via Fabro, with Codex/Claude corrections where\n  noted) and measured by deterministic tools. Engineering acceptance is pending human review.\n- The #1261, #250 and #560 branches conflict with each other upstream, and #560 conflicts with\n  the #490 draft. Rebase whichever merges later.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
